WEBVTT

00:04.900 --> 00:07.070
And that's the entire process.

00:07.070 --> 00:09.280
Do you have any questions?

00:10.140 --> 00:14.620
Come to think of it, is that black-haired
researcher I met last time absent?

00:15.580 --> 00:19.580
You mean Sei? She's working elsewhere today.

00:19.580 --> 00:21.870
Is that so? I see.

00:22.370 --> 00:24.050
Thank you very much.

00:27.500 --> 00:32.720
I feel bad asking the same question again, 
but is Sei here today?

00:33.200 --> 00:36.680
I'm very sorry. She's busy 
working on another project...

00:38.680 --> 00:41.190
Hello. Is Sei...

00:41.500 --> 00:44.650
I'm sorry. She's still...

00:46.170 --> 00:46.860
Today—

00:46.860 --> 00:48.130
Unfortunately not!

00:50.760 --> 00:51.930
Is Sei here?

00:53.870 --> 00:56.000
I can't do this anymore!

00:56.000 --> 01:00.450
Every time he comes,
he keeps asking and asking and asking for Sei!

01:00.450 --> 01:03.540
I can only lie to him for so long!

01:04.050 --> 01:09.830
Isn't Prince Ten'yuu being monitored by 
the knights assigned to him as bodyguards?

01:09.830 --> 01:14.120
Indeed. He can no longer get lost 
while going for a walk.

01:14.120 --> 01:18.470
Who knew he'd simply resort
to asking after you to find you?

01:18.470 --> 01:25.440
It's difficult to refuse a prince 
going through the proper channels...

01:28.660 --> 01:33.160
Do you think he knows that I'm avoiding him?

01:33.490 --> 01:36.120
I'd be surprised if he didn't.

01:36.120 --> 01:37.620
Of course...

01:38.160 --> 01:41.530
Sorry for putting you through all this, Jude.

01:41.530 --> 01:46.090
I don't mind, but I think we've
milked it about as much as we can.

01:46.630 --> 01:49.550
Do you think the prince will ever relent?

01:53.500 --> 01:55.010
I suppose we've no recourse.

01:57.470 --> 01:58.970
Yup, <i>we'll</i> give up.

01:59.760 --> 02:00.980
Come again?

03:48.020 --> 03:50.200
I see she's here today.

03:50.200 --> 03:51.590
Looks like it.

03:56.110 --> 04:01.350
<i>Now that we've crossed paths, I can't
 realistically keep avoiding him forever.</i>

04:01.770 --> 04:04.230
<i>I'll take care not to expose my identity.</i>

04:06.410 --> 04:08.140
Hello, Sei.

04:09.990 --> 04:11.110
Your Highness!

04:12.760 --> 04:15.040
Welcome to the Institute.

04:16.220 --> 04:18.170
I'm very happy to meet you again.

04:18.560 --> 04:20.610
No, the pleasure's all mine.

04:23.910 --> 04:25.790
That's quite a sum...

04:26.140 --> 04:29.740
We also prepare the potions 
for the royal palace here.

04:30.360 --> 04:32.460
That must be challenging work.

04:32.460 --> 04:34.960
How many of you did it take 
to make this many?

04:34.960 --> 04:35.800
Huh?

04:36.420 --> 04:37.320
Huh?

04:40.140 --> 04:44.810
Let me think.
 Probably four... or five people?

04:45.720 --> 04:49.560
<i>That was close! I can't tell him 
I made all of these myself!</i>

04:50.230 --> 04:51.500
I see.

04:51.500 --> 04:54.280
Are these all mid-grade potions?

04:54.280 --> 04:56.280
Yes. I'm surprised you can tell.

04:58.740 --> 05:00.860
It seems like the basic steps to brew them

05:00.860 --> 05:03.320
are no different than the methods of Zaidera.

05:03.320 --> 05:05.780
Oh, is that so?

05:06.470 --> 05:08.920
<i>He can tell just by looking at them?</i>

05:08.920 --> 05:12.010
<i>Like I thought, he really knows his stuff.</i>

05:13.050 --> 05:18.200
However, the potions we use to cure
 status ailments are somewhat different.

05:18.200 --> 05:19.550
How so?

05:20.160 --> 05:24.290
I believe it's due to the differing flora
 between Zaidera and Salutania.

05:24.290 --> 05:27.560
Our recipes use many medicinal herbs 
not available here.

05:28.160 --> 05:30.930
Medicinal herbs unique to Zaidera?

05:51.540 --> 05:55.500
<i>I-I couldn't help getting absorbed 
in our medicinal herb discussion!</i>

05:55.500 --> 05:58.960
My apologies! I've kept you so long.

05:59.420 --> 06:02.690
No, I had forgotten the time.

06:03.380 --> 06:07.830
The depth of your knowledge is profound. 
I have learned a lot from you.

06:12.220 --> 06:17.190
By the way, does this facility 
make any high-grade potions?

06:19.390 --> 06:21.190
High-grade potions?

06:22.060 --> 06:26.740
For instance, ones that might have
 the power to remedy an ailment

06:26.740 --> 06:29.330
that cannot be treated with other potions?

06:31.510 --> 06:33.710
What gave you that idea?

06:34.560 --> 06:35.420
Well...

06:36.120 --> 06:41.480
Earlier, you told me several researchers
 worked on this sum of potions.

06:41.480 --> 06:43.880
Even so, it's a staggering amount.

06:44.600 --> 06:46.060
Y-Yes...

06:46.510 --> 06:49.920
If you can regularly produce
 this kind of output,

06:49.920 --> 06:53.350
I thought someone here might be
capable of crafting high-grade potions.

06:56.000 --> 06:59.770
This is just a guess, 
but perhaps you might be...

06:59.770 --> 07:04.380
It's true that I know someone 
who can make high-grade potions.

07:04.380 --> 07:07.490
However, they fail more than they succeed.

07:07.980 --> 07:09.870
They do?

07:10.430 --> 07:14.750
As you know, the ingredients for high-grade 
potions are quite costly

07:14.750 --> 07:17.070
and it's hard to recoup the expense.

07:17.070 --> 07:19.980
And given the low chances of success,

07:19.980 --> 07:22.840
they're difficult to make regularly.

07:22.840 --> 07:27.300
I see. We face a similar 
problem in my homeland.

07:27.740 --> 07:34.730
So I may occasionally receive 
high-grade potions from my acquaintance,

07:34.730 --> 07:38.270
but I could hardly rise to the 
challenge making them myself.

07:38.710 --> 07:42.980
I see. It seems I was mistaken...

07:45.740 --> 07:47.890
Thank you for your time today.

07:48.350 --> 07:49.490
Don't mention it.

07:49.490 --> 07:50.790
Until next time...

07:56.160 --> 07:59.170
"Purpose"

08:01.120 --> 08:04.710
That was so exhausting!

08:05.250 --> 08:07.170
You did a fantastic job today.

08:07.650 --> 08:10.640
Looks like this is even more 
taxing than your usual work!

08:10.640 --> 08:12.670
Not physically.

08:13.020 --> 08:16.850
Actually, talking with His Highness
was rather interesting.

08:16.850 --> 08:19.420
You guys <i>did</i> seem pretty into it.

08:19.690 --> 08:22.200
Seems like you really hit it off.

08:22.200 --> 08:24.550
Th-That was a part of my plan!

08:24.550 --> 08:25.890
Oh?

08:28.050 --> 08:32.120
But that's why it's so painful to lie to him.

08:32.570 --> 08:34.830
Sorry you have to do this for the kingdom.

08:35.200 --> 08:39.790
Don't say that. This is just part
of my duties, if you think about it.

08:40.090 --> 08:44.000
Still, I wonder why Prince Ten'yuu 
is so fixated on you.

08:44.730 --> 08:47.710
He probably wants to know more 
about the Holy Saint.

08:48.180 --> 08:51.950
Perhaps he's just quenching 
a thirst for knowledge.

08:51.950 --> 08:55.490
On the other hand, he could 
be gauging your use in war.

08:56.390 --> 09:00.400
Well, a Holy Saint <i>can</i> be 
useful in all sorts of ways.

09:00.400 --> 09:01.270
Hey.

09:01.930 --> 09:04.870
Well, no point taking stabs in the dark.

09:04.870 --> 09:08.060
More importantly, we need 
to focus on how to handle him.

09:08.060 --> 09:09.740
You're right.

09:09.740 --> 09:16.200
After him suspiciously "getting lost,"
 it doesn't hurt to be wary.

09:16.660 --> 09:19.910
So we'll continue to proceed with caution?

09:21.420 --> 09:26.400
That Sei is our Holy Saint 
and there are things only she can do...

09:26.400 --> 09:30.380
These two facts must be kept secret.

09:33.270 --> 09:36.510
We may need to collect 
some intelligence ourselves.

09:36.510 --> 09:37.600
Intelligence?

09:37.600 --> 09:42.100
Yes. Don't they say that offense 
is the best defense?

10:10.290 --> 10:13.610
An illustrated book on the flora of Zaidera?

10:13.610 --> 10:17.260
I think we can manage to get something 
like that. What do you need it for?

10:17.870 --> 10:21.550
A guest from Zaidera 
is visiting the royal palace.

10:21.550 --> 10:23.840
Oh, the imperial prince.

10:23.840 --> 10:24.840
That's right.

10:24.840 --> 10:27.960
He likes to ask me lots of questions,

10:27.960 --> 10:31.680
and I thought I might keep the heat off me
by steering our conversations

10:31.680 --> 10:34.450
toward medicinal herbs from his homeland.

10:35.750 --> 10:37.810
How very like you, Lady Sei.

10:38.340 --> 10:43.210
Are you sure this isn't just an excuse 
to learn about herbs from Zaidera?

10:43.210 --> 10:45.170
I-I don't know what you're talking about...

10:46.960 --> 10:51.380
Anyway, can the imperial prince 
keep up with you intellectually?

10:51.720 --> 10:54.680
Yes, he seems very
 knowledgeable on the subject.

10:54.680 --> 10:57.160
There was practically
 no end to our conversation.

10:57.160 --> 11:01.470
I think his studies are heavily 
focused on medicinal plants.

11:02.720 --> 11:04.180
So that's how it shakes out...

11:04.860 --> 11:06.140
How it shakes out?

11:08.650 --> 11:12.610
Well, you see, my lady,
 it's quite suspicious.

11:13.160 --> 11:14.950
What do you mean?

11:15.380 --> 11:19.660
Something has been bothering me 
about the imperial prince.

11:21.480 --> 11:26.080
Lady Sei, do you remember meeting 
Captain Ceyran in Morgenhaffen?

11:30.180 --> 11:31.840
What about him?

11:31.840 --> 11:35.250
Well, he was searching for an alchemist.

11:35.250 --> 11:38.140
One who can make high-grade potions.

11:39.850 --> 11:42.430
We didn't know anything at the time.

11:43.560 --> 11:48.680
We've looked into Captain 
Ceyran a bit since then.

11:48.680 --> 11:52.150
He apparently has a very powerful backer.

11:52.760 --> 11:53.940
He does?

11:55.260 --> 12:00.300
The imperial prince who is currently here 
as an exchange student.

12:00.300 --> 12:03.670
His in-depth knowledge 
of plants makes me suspect

12:03.670 --> 12:08.460
that <i>he's</i> really the one
 looking for an alchemist.

12:08.460 --> 12:12.490
So Prince Ten'yuu is personally 
visiting various facilities

12:12.490 --> 12:14.920
while his subordinates search the cities?

12:14.920 --> 12:17.210
But it's strange...

12:21.510 --> 12:25.810
While we were conducting business,
I spoke with Captain Ceyran personally.

12:26.280 --> 12:28.630
I brought up the Holy Saint,

12:28.630 --> 12:31.400
and he couldn't have cared less.

12:31.850 --> 12:34.360
You sure he wasn't pretending?

12:34.360 --> 12:39.770
Yeah, he showed no interest whatsoever
and simply changed the subject.

12:39.770 --> 12:42.320
All he cares about is finding an alchemist.

12:42.800 --> 12:46.310
He seems to believe that the Holy Saint's power

12:46.310 --> 12:50.390
is good for subjugating monsters
and nothing more.

12:50.390 --> 12:55.790
We've spoken with others from Zaidera,
and they're all under the same impression.

12:56.110 --> 12:57.710
Hold on a second there!

12:58.430 --> 13:03.820
This means Ceyran is probably
looking for an alchemist for Prince Ten'yuu,

13:03.820 --> 13:07.720
who is so desperate that
he came to the palace himself...

13:07.720 --> 13:10.690
But his goal isn't the Holy Saint.

13:11.540 --> 13:15.900
They just need someone 
who's really good at making potions?

13:16.900 --> 13:20.240
That is our conclusion.

13:20.240 --> 13:22.990
Why would a foreign prince go so far?

13:22.990 --> 13:25.440
High-grade potions are rare,

13:25.440 --> 13:29.560
but he'd have a better chance 
of finding them in his own country.

13:29.560 --> 13:31.830
That's the mystery.

13:32.500 --> 13:36.560
Well, at the very least,
 he doesn't seem to have ill intent

13:36.560 --> 13:38.760
toward our Holy Saint.

13:41.280 --> 13:45.180
Regardless of their intent, 
I have to say I'm curious now.

13:51.700 --> 13:54.350
Okay, I'm going to do a little digging.

13:54.350 --> 13:55.450
Huh?

13:58.190 --> 14:00.730
Digging? On the imperial prince?

14:00.730 --> 14:02.780
Isn't that dangerous?

14:02.780 --> 14:06.010
Prince Ten'yuu is here
 to study for a full year.

14:06.720 --> 14:13.000
It'll be exhausting to lie to him the 
entire time. I'm truly not good at it.

14:13.360 --> 14:14.380
But...

14:14.380 --> 14:16.460
Do you have a plan?

14:16.970 --> 14:20.350
I have a dependable partner
 who's a kindred spirit!

14:40.540 --> 14:42.360
She should be here soon.

14:44.040 --> 14:45.010
Liz!

14:45.260 --> 14:46.780
Or not!

14:49.840 --> 14:52.250
Should I not have come?

14:53.460 --> 14:55.750
Th-That's not it! I'm sorry!

14:55.750 --> 14:57.790
Liz... Er, Elizabeth...

14:57.790 --> 15:01.960
I mean, Lady Ashley and I
have an appointment.

15:01.960 --> 15:04.670
I see. Will you be reading together?

15:05.070 --> 15:08.080
It's more like a strategy meeting...

15:08.630 --> 15:10.890
What brings you here, Commander Hawke?

15:11.350 --> 15:15.570
In truth, I'll be returning home
for some time next week.

15:15.570 --> 15:17.520
Returning home?

15:17.520 --> 15:22.480
Monster sightings have become 
more prevalent in Hawke territory.

15:22.850 --> 15:24.440
That's...

15:25.860 --> 15:27.640
It's nothing so dire.

15:28.040 --> 15:33.150
Just an excuse of sorts for a son
 to visit his parents.

15:33.540 --> 15:37.870
But our home is quite far 
from the royal capital.

15:39.950 --> 15:43.070
I'm afraid I'll be away for a while.

15:43.070 --> 15:46.930
So I wanted to see you before I departed.

15:50.120 --> 15:51.030
Oh?

15:53.680 --> 15:54.870
Oh my!

15:54.870 --> 15:56.140
Dearie me.

15:56.530 --> 15:58.600
Liz! Liz!

15:58.600 --> 16:03.460
My apologies. I just recalled 
that I have something to do.

16:03.460 --> 16:04.780
Liz?!

16:05.110 --> 16:11.120
Why don't you discuss your plans
 with Lord Hawke instead?

16:12.580 --> 16:15.320
Good day, Sei. Take your time.

16:15.660 --> 16:18.310
Liz!

16:23.360 --> 16:25.260
What plans?

16:25.260 --> 16:28.340
W-Well, about that...

16:31.220 --> 16:35.770
I would love nothing more
 than to help you out if I can.

16:36.710 --> 16:37.890
Sure...

16:40.480 --> 16:42.140
I see.

16:42.140 --> 16:44.600
You wish to know Prince Ten'yuu's purpose,

16:44.600 --> 16:48.950
but you feel like asking him directly 
may cause a diplomatic issue.

16:50.790 --> 16:55.330
He's particularly interested 
in potions that can cure ailments,

16:55.330 --> 16:58.610
but I don't exactly know why that is.

16:58.610 --> 17:02.670
So I'd like to find out more in that regard.

17:03.030 --> 17:06.630
Is that the reason for all these 
technical books? Quite impressive.

17:06.970 --> 17:10.460
Yet I still don't know
 how to bring it up with him.

17:10.460 --> 17:14.850
I feel like he'll deflect my questions 
if I ask him too frankly.

17:18.710 --> 17:21.730
In that case, what about this?

17:37.780 --> 17:38.830
Your Highness!

17:39.780 --> 17:44.290
I wanted to thank you for always 
taking time out of your workdays for me.

17:45.870 --> 17:50.220
Starting next week, I will be 
visiting a different facility.

17:50.830 --> 17:52.510
I see...

17:52.510 --> 17:56.680
I really enjoyed discussing 
medicinal herbs with you.

17:59.030 --> 18:03.160
As did I. I've never met someone 
as knowledgeable as you are before.

18:03.840 --> 18:05.860
I'm honored.

18:06.480 --> 18:09.810
While our conversations 
have been quite fruitful,

18:09.810 --> 18:13.320
I'm afraid I don't have long left.

18:13.770 --> 18:15.530
You don't have long?

18:16.480 --> 18:17.990
Is Sei here?

18:19.800 --> 18:20.950
Commander Hawke!

18:26.630 --> 18:28.620
I have a request.

18:28.620 --> 18:30.090
What is it?

18:32.120 --> 18:34.820
Our inventory has gotten quite low.

18:35.180 --> 18:39.180
We'd like more potions 
that can cure status ailments.

18:39.670 --> 18:41.760
What kind are you looking for?

18:41.760 --> 18:45.020
High-grades ones.
The kind most people can't make.

18:45.020 --> 18:47.860
Don't you know an alchemist who can help me?

18:49.470 --> 18:51.580
I can't really say for certain.

18:51.580 --> 18:53.880
With high-grade potion for ailments,

18:53.880 --> 18:57.160
the difficulty varies depending 
on what you want to cure.

18:57.160 --> 19:00.990
What types of conditions
 are the hardest to treat?

19:00.990 --> 19:07.270
For instance, poisons circulating
 in the body that inhibit healing

19:07.270 --> 19:10.340
are challenging to remedy
 with regular potions.

19:10.340 --> 19:11.660
I see.

19:11.660 --> 19:15.670
I've heard ailments that present
 differently from person to person

19:15.670 --> 19:19.050
are also especially hard to craft potions for.

19:19.470 --> 19:20.580
Understood.

19:20.580 --> 19:24.770
But even so, isn't the alchemist you know
talented enough to deliver?

19:25.080 --> 19:29.480
Yes, I'm sure they'd try their best to help.

19:29.930 --> 19:32.600
They've saved so many lives already.

19:32.600 --> 19:38.200
I'm sure their talent is far 
more special than they believe.

19:39.840 --> 19:42.870
Well, I don't know about that...

19:44.880 --> 19:53.050
Now then, isn't your friend keenly interested
in creating potions for various ailments?

19:53.050 --> 19:55.230
Yes, that's right.

19:55.230 --> 19:58.430
Although their success will depend
 on what they're trying to treat.

19:58.980 --> 20:02.920
I'll return once I have a better idea
 of exactly what our unit needs.

20:09.080 --> 20:11.100
<i>Looks like that worked, I think.</i>

20:12.270 --> 20:15.280
I'll submit my request some other time, then.

20:15.930 --> 20:17.490
I'll be waiting.

20:18.770 --> 20:22.870
I want to see you 
when I come back, after all.

20:25.710 --> 20:26.870
If you'll excuse me...

20:29.830 --> 20:34.600
<i>Goodness, we didn't 
rehearse any lines like that!</i>

20:37.470 --> 20:40.970
And so, we put on a little act.

20:41.420 --> 20:43.750
You really do some daring things.

20:47.140 --> 20:50.030
Sei? His Highness wants to speak with you.

20:50.690 --> 20:52.220
Here we go!

21:01.680 --> 21:07.400
Forgive me. I happened 
to overhear your conversation before.

21:07.400 --> 21:09.500
Which conversation do you mean?

21:11.690 --> 21:16.710
Could you possibly introduce me 
to your alchemist friend, Sei?

21:19.060 --> 21:21.680
They're very particular...

21:22.350 --> 21:26.010
What exactly are you hoping for from them?

21:28.710 --> 21:31.370
Will you keep this information a secret?

21:36.120 --> 21:38.370
Have you ever heard 
of someone slowly wasting,

21:38.370 --> 21:41.690
eventually unable to use their arms and legs?

21:42.630 --> 21:47.620
Well, I've heard of diseases 
that cause muscular atrophy.

21:48.210 --> 21:52.210
I'm looking for a potion 
that can cure such an ailment.

21:52.740 --> 21:55.590
No alchemist in Zaidera 
could do anything for it.

21:57.220 --> 21:59.510
I know someone suffering from the condition.

22:01.080 --> 22:03.000
It's my mother.

23:35.020 --> 23:40.020
"Divine Blessing"

23:35.020 --> 23:40.590
Next Time
